   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the financing and construction of facilities by the dormitory authority for Summit Educational Resource, Inc., of Western New York",
    "basePrintNo": "S6461",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6461-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1676 & 1680, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6461\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the\nfinancing and construction of facilities by the dormitory authority\nfor Summit Educational Resource, Inc., of Western New York\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nTo enable Summit Educational Resource, Inc., of Western New York, a\nnot-for-profit organization, to obtain funding and enter into\ncontracts through the dormitory authority, for the acquisition,\nfinancing and/or refinancing, design, construction, renovation,\nreconstruction, development, improvement, furnishing, expansion and/or\nequipping of a facility or facilities and necessary ancillary and\nrelated facilities.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 amends paragraph (b) of subdivision 2 of section 1676 of the\npublic authorities law by adding a new undesignated subparagraph\nincluding Summit Educational Resource, Inc., of Western New York, a\nnot-for-profit organization, in the list of entities deemed to be a\n\"dormitory\".\n\nSection 2 amends subdivision 1 of section 1680 of the public\nauthorities law by adding a new undesignated paragraph including\nSummit Educational Resource, Inc., of Western New York, a\nnot-for-profit organization, in the list of entities deemed to be an\n\"educational institution\".\n\nSection 3 provides that any contracts entered into by the dormitory\nauthority pursuant to this act shall be deemed state contracts.\n\nSection 4 provides that this act shall take effect immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nSummit Educational Resource, Inc., of Western New York, is a private,\nnot-for-profit organization formed to provide early intervention &\neducation, behavioral health, community, and adult programs and\nservices to children and adults. In 1973, Nancy Harris, founder of\nSummit, was interested in expanding the speech and language skills of\nher son who was born with a severe hearing loss. She strongly believed\nthat children with communication disorders could best develop\nmeaningful speech and language during their everyday experiences, and\ndeveloped a program for four children in the kitchen of her\nWilliamsville home. In 2005, Summit opened a state-of-the-art school\nin Amherst, New York. In September 2009, Summit opened the new Paddock\nVocational Training Center on Creekside Drive to serve the needs of\nstudents ages 17 - 21. Today, Summit has grown to a staff of nearly\n600 full-time, part-time and contractual employees dedicated to\nserving Western New York children and adults each year with autism and\nother developmental disabilities. The funding apparatus of the\nDormitory Authority will significantly enhance the organization's\nability to achieve its goals.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
